{"explanation":"Encryptor now resolves a persistent AndroidKeyStore-generated current wrapping key under a distinct alias for all new writes, while retaining the legacy master-key lookup path. The current-key resolver deliberately does not supply caller-generated GCM parameters: the AndroidKeyStore provider must generate encryption parameters for its randomized-encryption-required key, and EncryptedKey retains the provider-created parameters in the current record.","review_assumptions":["The coordinated MasterKey change uses the same persistent current wrapping-key alias, "currentMasterKey", and compatible AndroidKeyStore AES-GCM generation parameters.","The Android minimum/runtime API level supports KeyGenParameterSpec and AndroidKeyStore AES-GCM keys.","EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey, String) initializes current AndroidKeyStore encryption without caller-supplied GCM parameters and persists the provider-generated Cipher parameters.","Encryptor currently exposes no encrypted-record decryption entry point; the retained getLegacyWrappingKey lookup preserves resolution of the established "masterKey" alias for a legacy read path when one is present."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","original_code":"import android.security.keystore.KeyProperties;
import android.security.keystore.KeyProtection;","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"import android.security.keystore.KeyGenParameterSpec;
import android.security.keystore.KeyProperties;
import android.security.keystore.KeyProtection;","reason":"Import the AndroidKeyStore key-generation parameter type required to create the persistent current AES-GCM wrapping key.","symbol":"AndroidKeyStore imports"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","original_code":"import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
